{"paper": "RRB-GroupD-28-Nov-2025-Shift1.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "answer-anchored", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 25, "tagged_count": 20, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "If A : B = 1 : 3, B : C = 4 : 3 and C : D = 6 : 7, then A : B : C : D is:", "options": [{"text": "8 : 22 : 18 : 21", "added": false}, {"text": "6 : 24 : 18 : 21", "added": false}, {"text": "8 : 24 : 18 : 21", "added": false}, {"text": "8 : 24 : 16 : 21", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "mp-sp-relation", "key_answer": "8%"}, {"n": 2, "text": "A train, 1312 m long, is running at a speed of 54 m/s. If it takes 106 seconds to cross a tunnel, then find the length of the tunnel.", "options": [{"text": "4402 m", "added": false}, {"text": "4413 m", "added": false}, {"text": "4412 m", "added": false}, {"text": "4408 m", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trains", "sub": "train-vs-platform", "key_answer": "4412 m"}, {"n": 3, "text": "Which of the following numbers is divisible by 7?", "options": [{"text": "7357306", "added": false}, {"text": "7132951", "added": false}, {"text": "7660778", "added": false}, {"text": "6825907", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "divisibility-rules", "key_answer": "7132951"}, {"n": 4, "text": "The average of 6.5, 10.6, 19.7 and a is 12. The value of a is:1640", "options": [{"text": "11.2", "added": false}, {"text": "10.2", "added": false}, {"text": "12.2", "added": false}, {"text": "13.2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": "11.2"}, {"n": 5, "text": "If A : B = 1 : 3, B : C = 4 : 3 and C : D = 6 : 7, then A : B : C : D is:", "options": [{"text": "8 : 22 : 18 : 21", "added": false}, {"text": "6 : 24 : 18 : 21", "added": false}, {"text": "8 : 24 : 18 : 21", "added": false}, {"text": "8 : 24 : 16 : 21", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": "8 : 24 : 18 : 21"}, {"n": 6, "text": "A father is 5 times as old as his son. If the sum of their ages is 54 years, how old is the son?", "options": [{"text": "11 years", "added": false}, {"text": "12 years", "added": false}, {"text": "9 years", "added": false}, {"text": "10 years", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Elementary Statistics", "sub": "mean-median-mode", "key_answer": "7"}, {"n": 7, "text": "After selling an article at a discount of 25%, the profit percentage obtained is 2%. What is the mark-up percentage?", "options": [{"text": "40%", "added": false}, {"text": "34%", "added": false}, {"text": "38%", "added": false}, {"text": "36%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ages", "sub": "present-age", "key_answer": "40 years"}, {"n": 8, "text": "A sum of money is to be distributed among A, B, C and D in the ratio of 10 : 7 : 9 : 5. If C gets ₹334 more than B, then how much did A receive?", "options": [{"text": "₹1,670", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,673", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,671", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,669", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": "₹1,670"}, {"n": 9, "text": "The area of a triangle is 61.5 m2. If one of its sides is 12.3 m, find the length of the perpendicular dropped on that side from the opposite vertex.", "options": [{"text": "11 m", "added": false}, {"text": "11.5 m", "added": false}, {"text": "10 m", "added": false}, {"text": "10.5 m", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "triangle-and-quadrilaterals", "key_answer": "10 m"}, {"n": 10, "text": "P is any point inside the rectangle ABCD. If PA = 85 cm, PB = 65 cm and PC = 5 cm, then the length of PD (in cm) is equal to:", "options": [{"text": "55", "added": false}, {"text": "58", "added": false}, {"text": "53", "added": false}, {"text": "51", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "quadrilaterals", "key_answer": "55"}, {"n": 11, "text": "The amount on a sum of ₹2,800 at 10% per annum compound interest, compounded annually, in 2 years will be:", "options": [{"text": "₹2,647", "added": false}, {"text": "₹3,604", "added": false}, {"text": "₹3,274", "added": false}, {"text": "₹3,388", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Compound Interest", "sub": "ci-formula", "key_answer": "₹3,388"}, {"n": 12, "text": "Sushma purchased a used car for ₹1,20,000 and spent ₹28,500 on its repairs. She then sold it to her friend Sam for ₹1,38,600. What percentage did she gain or lose? (Round off your answer to two decimal places.)", "options": [{"text": "8.67% loss", "added": false}, {"text": "6.67% loss", "added": false}, {"text": "5.38% gain", "added": false}, {"text": "6.67% gain", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": "6.67% loss"}, {"n": 13, "text": "The marked price of a wardrobe is ₹8,640, which is 35% above the cost price. It is sold at a discount of 20% on the marked price. Find the profit percentage.", "options": [{"text": "9%", "added": false}, {"text": "10%", "added": false}, {"text": "8%", "added": false}, {"text": "6%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ages", "sub": "present-age", "key_answer": "9 years"}, {"n": 14, "text": "Find the mode of the data 1, 11, 11, 8, 18, 8, 7, 7, 7, x, y, and 8, given that 3x + 7y = 42 and 7x + 3y = 58.", "options": [{"text": "11", "added": false}, {"text": "7", "added": false}, {"text": "18", "added": false}, {"text": "8", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "triangle-and-quadrilaterals", "key_answer": "B"}, {"n": 15, "text": "The price of oil is increased successively by 50% and then by 40%. What is the equivalent single percentage increase?", "options": [{"text": "90%", "added": false}, {"text": "75%", "added": false}, {"text": "100%", "added": false}, {"text": "110%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "successive-change", "key_answer": "110%"}, {"n": 16, "text": "The monthly incomes of two friends, Kiran and Mahesh, are in the ratio 5 : 8 respectively, and each of them saves ₹72,000 every month. If the ratio of their monthly expenditure is 2 : 4, find the monthly income of Kiran (in ₹).", "options": [{"text": "1,81,000", "added": false}, {"text": "2,52,000", "added": false}, {"text": "1,80,000", "added": false}, {"text": "1,79,000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "income-expenditure", "key_answer": "1,80,000"}, {"n": 17, "text": "Navya and Bhavya can paint a house in 40 days and 60 days, respectively. If they work on alternate days, starting with Bhavya, in how many days can the duo complete painting that house?", "options": [{"text": "45 days", "added": false}, {"text": "48 days", "added": false}, {"text": "50 days", "added": false}, {"text": "49 days", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "alternate-days", "key_answer": "48 days"}, {"n": 18, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "0", "added": false}, {"text": "0.5", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": "36"}, {"n": 19, "text": "A and B working together can do a piece of work in 6 days. B alone can do the same work in 9 days. How long (in days) will A alone take to do double the work?", "options": [{"text": "37", "added": false}, {"text": "18", "added": false}, {"text": "36", "added": false}, {"text": "39", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "mp-sp-relation", "key_answer": "36%"}, {"n": 20, "text": "After selling an article at a discount of 25%, the profit percentage obtained is 2%. What is the mark-up percentage?", "options": [{"text": "40%", "added": false}, {"text": "34%", "added": false}, {"text": "38%", "added": false}, {"text": "36%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "successive-change", "key_answer": "Increase by 10%"}]}